[2015.7s]   💬 ## M1 rework — addressed every critic point
[2015.7s]   💬 Comparing the original (mean 2.43) render against the reference exposed problems the small compare had hidden. I rebuilt against each note:
[2015.7s]   💬 - **Grade (was 1) — milky → low-key.** Added a compositor **RGB-curve crush** (black knee at 0.022 + gentle S) *before* the bloom, and dropped world/ambient near zero. Background now reads near-pure black (was a flat gray-green wash); mean 44, 0% clipped.
[2015.7s]   💬 - **Hero tower (was 1) — plain ziggurat → circuit-board.** Replaced the strength-only checker (which glowed uniform) with a **dark-body + bright-window MixShader** so real gridded windows read, reshaped it into a near-vertical monolith (was a smooth cone), and built a **structured crown + antenna + plume** instead of the blown orb.
[2015.7s]   💬 - **Emission clipping to cyan-white.** Dropped emission ~50%, shifted the hue off cyan into **deep saturated green** (low value / high saturation) — the crown no longer blows out; bloom carries the halo.
[2015.7s]   💬 - **Atmosphere (was 2) — flat band → turbulent nebula.** Root cause found by inspecting the volume graph: `stretch=(0.3,…)` scaled the noise to ~2 periods across the whole domain (a flat band), and a *deep* emissive domain averages to milk. Fixed with a **thin backdrop slab** (short light path → 2D turbulent clouds), isotropic `stretch=(1,1,1)`, punchy contrast, tiny emission, plus a tower-lit billow so the plume **blooms into** the haze.
[2015.7s]   💬 - **Palette — cyan/teal → silk-road green.** Reduced the blue channel across world tint, tower, crown and city lights.
[2015.7s]   💬 - **Depth (was 3) — flat uniform field.** Lowered the horizon, layered the city into **near/far tiers** with distance-scaled sizes, and packed a dense glittering carpet of tiny green + warm-white lights receding to the horizon.
[2015.7s]   💬 - **Motion (part of the 1).** Added a **downward push** to the dive (z 24→12) alongside the forward travel and CCW roll, and a longer shutter (0.45) so the roll/dive read as weighty continuous motion on frame 1.
[2015.7s]   💬 `build/M1.py` updated, re-run from an empty scene, and verified to reproduce this exact render (20 objects, camera keyed, frame 1). Scene stays lean (390 tris; all repeats instanced/scattered).
