[2620.0s]   💬 ## M1 rework #2 — every critic point addressed
[2620.0s]   💬 Reading the full-res `M1_r2.png` against the reference exposed the real gaps. I fixed each:
[2620.0s]   💬 - **Crush the blacks (grade was milky).** The milky upper wash was the emissive volume flooding uniformly. Rebuilt the world near-black (bg 0.008→0.003), dropped the volume emission, added a **harder crush curve** (toe knee 0.05 + steep S) and disabled AO fill. Upper frame is now deep black (20–22% pure black) with glow confined to the tower.
[2620.0s]   💬 - **Circuit-board megastructure (was a smooth obelisk).** Rebuilt the tower with **jagged setbacks, an asymmetric plan, 46 greeble protrusions**, and windows whose emission is **varied per-cell by a noise texture** — reads as architecture, not a lit block.
[2620.0s]   💬 - **Exploding crown burst (was a soft cap).** Replaced the cap with a **blooming mushroom of 118 emissive shards + a bright core**, blooming outward at the crown.
[2620.0s]   💬 - **Wispy nebula haze.** Solved the flat-band problem for good: near-unlit turbulent volume **lit by a bright green point light at the crown**, so the crown blooms green **into** structured clouds with black corners — plus faint corner fill and low ground fog.
[2620.0s]   💬 - **Grade contrast/bloom.** Steepened contrast, crushed the toe, and **tightened the bloom radius** (0.8→0.5) for disciplined glow.
[2620.0s]   💬 - **Low aerial reframe.** Tilted the camera down (89.3°→87.5°) and lowered it into a dive so the tower sits larger with dark sky above; added a **downward push** (z 33→16) to the forward+roll move.
[2620.0s]   💬 - **Emerald green (was lime/teal).** Retuned tower/crown/light hues to a richer silk-road emerald with varied tower emission.
[2620.0s]   💬 - **Ground depth.** Split lesser towers into **bright-near / dim-far tiers** and added **distance fog** so the light field falls off toward the horizon instead of a flat carpet.
[2620.0s]   💬 `build/M1.py` fully rewritten, re-run from an empty scene, and verified to reproduce this exact render (21 objects incl. the crown light, camera keyed, frame 1). Scene stays lean (~2.3k tris; all repeats instanced/scattered).
